module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a check's subject is narrower than the claim it is cited for** (EVERY DEGREE OF FREEDOM IN A CHECK'S SUBJECT -- which call sites, which spellings, which lexical states, which domain, which files -- is a place its coverage can silently be narrower than the population it is read as covering. ",

    "INVALID STATE: an executing, reached, green check whose declared subject is a strict superset of the population its implementation actually ranges over. ",

    "RUNG: outside the ladder, because the gap is invisible from the check's own result -- a wall whose range is too narrow is green for the same reason a wall over a clean corpus is green, and DESIGN section 4b(1) reads a class's rung as the MINIMUM across its in-scope paths, so a check like this INFLATES the rung of everything it is cited for. ",

    "THE ROUTE IS WHAT MAKES IT INVISIBLE: the narrowing is never a decision, it is the shape of the first implementation -- an author edits one file, so the scanner reads one file; the corpus spells the call one way, so the seed matches one spelling; the fixture has no raw strings, so the projection has no raw-string state; the window is never short, so the universal is never vacuous. ",

    "Each is locally reasonable and none is written down, which is why the gap survives the review that reads the check's LOGIC and never asks what its INPUT was. ",

    "SPECIMEN, and the reason this is a class rather than a bug: ONE guard in PR #10033 carried SIX instances -- (1) a body-local grep for the mutator, defeated by moving the call one helper deeper; (2) a seed matching only the fully-qualified path, defeated by `use std::env;`; (3) a lexical projection with no raw-string state, so an unbalanced brace in a fixture silently shifted every containment decision after it; (4) `take(n).all(..)`, vacuously true over a short remainder (rostered as predicate_vacuously_true_on_an_empty_domain); (5) a scan ranging over ONE FILE while the scope declaration claimed every test the required lane runs -- found by review, not by the author; and (6) after widening, cross-file call edges resolved by BARE NAME, which merges every declaration of a shared spelling (18 `main`s in that crate) and bridged one production seed into hundreds of unrelated tests. ",

    "Four were found by the author, one by review, one by the widening itself, and the sixth is the mirror of the fifth: over-broad and under-broad are the same defect measured in opposite directions, and both are reported as coverage. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: name the check's SUBJECT and the check's RANGE as two separate sentences, then ask what is in the first and not the second. ",

    "If the answer is anything, the claim is the narrower one until the range is widened. ",

    "The review-side tell is a scope comment that quantifies (`every test`, `all modules`, `any call site`) beside an implementation that names ONE input. ",

    "BOUNDED AGAINST TWO NEIGHBOURS. ",

    "selection_view_read_as_population is a set produced by a MEASUREMENT threshold and read as the population, arriving as the fix for a real objection; here nothing is measured and nothing is filtered -- the range was simply never as wide as the sentence beside it. ",

    "incidental_denominator_as_wall is a guard that holds by an upstream coincidence that genuinely holds; here the guard holds over a population it never read. ",

    "CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed and decidable, BUT SCOPED TO THIS CLASS'S EXECUTING FORMS AND NOT TO THE CLASS (scope amended when the ninth form landed): a check whose subject is a VALUE it receives rather than a scope its implementation re-derives cannot range over less than it claims, because the claim and the range are then one object. ",

    "That derivation needs an executing check with an input. Every form above it is one, so the limit was never visible and the ceiling read as belonging to the class when it belongs to a sub-case: where the subject is a WRITTEN SURFACE a human is supposed to read completely, the claim and the range stay TWO objects and cannot inherit this ceiling. The ninth form below is that sub-case and carries no rung of its own. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as a capability: the guarded population is passed to the check as a constructed value carrying its own extent, sufficient that no check can name a subject its input does not contain. ",

    "WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: that widening always wins. ",

    "Narrowing the DECLARATION to match the range is equally honest and is sometimes correct -- what is forbidden is leaving the two different, and the choice between them is a cost measurement, not a preference. ",

    "On this specimen widening cost one change of input plus one linear-time rewrite of a quadratic edge builder, and the wider check ran FASTER than the narrow one, which is what settled it.) A SEVENTH FORM, AND THE FIRST WHERE THE NARROWING IS AN AXIS OF THE COMPARISON RATHER THAN A RANGE OF INPUTS (2026-09-03). ",

    "The six above narrow WHICH INPUTS a check sees; this one narrows WHAT IT COMPARES, so it is invisible even over a complete corpus. ",

    "`v1_compiler.behavioral_receipt_host` `behavioral_differential` is cited as the executing evidence for DESIGN section 7 behavioural equivalence, and its own doc comment cites section 7 by name. ",

    "What it RANGES OVER is the seed-Rust versus emitted-Rust axis: `generate_receipt_driver` emits a Rust main that prints each planned call, and the differential runs that ONE driver twice -- against the tree as committed, then after the candidate overwrites its mirror and the crate is rebuilt. ",

    "Both transcripts come from COMPILED RUST BINARIES, so any property the two realizations SHARE is unobservable to it by construction, however clean the corpus. ",

    "THE DISCRIMINATING INSTANCE IS NOT THIS ROW'S TO STATE, AND CITING IT RATHER THAN RESTATING IT IS THE POINT (amended 2026-09-03). ",

    "The interpreter-versus-emitted evaluation divergence has an owner with better evidence than prose: `realization_arms_diverge_on_whether_the_program_refuses`, filed by gunbc#10139, which carries the source reading in both directions AND an EXECUTED red -- `fn guarded_division(n: Int) -> Bool { n != 0 && (100 / n) > 1 }`, run and dated, explicitly not asserted. ",

    "An earlier draft of this receipt described that divergence in its own words. ",

    "That would have been a second authority for a fact this ledger already owns, committed inside the row about subjects narrower than their claims, which is the specimen writing itself. ",

    "WHAT IS THIS ROW'S OWN SUBJECT is the other half and a different fact: THE INSTRUMENT CANNOT SEE IT. ",

    "Both of `behavioral_differential`'s arms are compiled Rust, so they share the target's evaluation semantics and agree with each other -- wrongly, together -- on exactly the inputs where that cited class occurs. ",

    "The divergence is #10139's; the blindness of the equivalence instrument to it is this row's. ",

    "THE REVIEW TELL FOR THIS FORM: ask what the two sides of a comparison SHARE, not what the check ranges over -- a differential between two realizations of one target cannot see a property of that target. ",

    "The ordinary tell, a green over a population nobody checked, is unavailable here: this instrument is green for a reason no input can change. ",

    "ONE NEIGHBOUR CHECKED AND EXCLUDED, so the next reader does not re-derive it: `v2.compiler.emit_host` `run_test_claim_emit_vs_eval` IS enrolled on the required floor and DOES pair an executed emitted answer with an interpreted one, with a positive control and a discriminating negative. ",

    "But it evaluates `expected_eval_root` while host-running the emitted `claim_input_root` -- two different roots -- so it is an ORACLE comparison and the interpreter never evaluates the expression the target runs. ",

    "Its subject excludes same-expression evaluation divergence structurally, not by coverage. ",

    "THE AUTHOR'S OWN INSTANCE, recorded because it happened while filing this: the first draft claimed NO required phase pairs an interpreted answer with an emitted-and-executed one, derived by enumerating the closed five-variant `RequiredCiPhase` and then asserting what its members execute without reading them. ",

    "The population was closed; the claim about its members was never checked -- a real enumeration, divided by nothing. ",

    "It was refuted by the very rows that refused the pull request being worked on.AN EIGHTH FORM, AND THE FIRST WHERE THE BLIND SPOT IS NOT ARBITRARY BUT CORRELATED WITH RECENCY (2026-09-03, tidy-koi-619 on gunbc#10106, with warm-seal-35 as the finder). ",

    "Every form above treats the narrowing as ARBITRARY -- 'never a decision, the shape of the first implementation'. ",

    "When the narrowed axis is a DIRECTION over a time-ordered subject, the narrowing stops being arbitrary and starts tracking recency, which makes it strictly worse than a random miss. ",

    "THE INSTANCE: a squash-merged branch survives as a divergent-looking branch and auto-opens a pull request that would REVERT main. ",

    "Diagnosing gunbc#10242 I enumerated what a merge would wrongly RE-ADD -- 47 namespace admissions consumed by their own merge, plus three files deleted on main -- and concluded, in the comment closing it, 'there is no file where this branch carries content main wants'. ",

    "THAT SENTENCE IS TRUE. ",

    "Its subject is one direction; its reading is completeness. ",

    "The 54 differing paths were 43 common-but-differing, 3 branch-only which a merge RE-ADDS, and 8 main-only which a merge DELETES -- and the deletion category, which the sweep never ranged over, contained a witness test that had landed twenty minutes earlier. ",

    "WHY RECENCY MAKES IT WORSE: the newest work on main is NECESSARILY in the merge-would-delete category, because the more recently something landed the more certain it is to be absent from a superseded branch. ",

    "So this sweep's blind spot is not spread evenly over the population -- it concentrates on exactly the rows that are newest, least recoverable, and least likely to be noticed missing, since nobody is yet watching for the absence of a thing that landed twenty minutes ago. ",

    "A check whose miss probability rises with the value of what is missed is a different economic object from one that misses uniformly, and the review tell is different too: it is not 'what population did this range over' but 'is the missed set correlated with anything, and with what'. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE FOR THIS FORM: when a check's subject is a COMPARISON between two states, name both directions as separate sentences and range over both -- present-on-A-absent-on-B and present-on-B-absent-on-A are two populations, and a size or presence heuristic run one way answers only one of them. ",

    "WHY IT IS FILED HERE AND NOT AS ITS OWN CLASS: three instances arrived within one day from three unrelated angles -- a record comparator that could not parse a parameterized constructor and so reported None == None as agreement on the `standing` field; an assert-count-is-1 guard over a citation sweep that held because the PATTERN was narrow rather than because the file was clean; and this one-directional diff sweep. ",

    "The author's first instinct was to mint a new class around the sentence 'a check that does not state its own denominator cannot be distinguished from a complete one'. ",

    "That sentence is this row's INVALID STATE restated, so a new row would have been a second authority for a rostered fact -- the DESIGN section 2 failed decomposition, committed inside the ledger that exists to prevent it, which is the same self-demonstration the seventh form records. ",

    "The class was already here; only the recency observation was new. ",

    "A NINTH FORM, WHERE THE SUBJECT ITSELF MOVED UNDER THE CHECK (2026-09-05, adjudicated in jolly-dove-86, measured on gunbc#10552). It is numbered ninth because this row already carried an eighth; the brief that commissioned it said eighth, and the row is the authority on its own count. ",

    "STATEMENT: a repair changes the SUBJECT that the earlier observation described. Completeness and correctness must be established against the FINAL SUBJECT, with the selection boundary explicit; finding the newly inserted wording is not that establishment. ",

    "THE REASONING UNDER IT: checked revision A, plus edit A to B, does not equal checked revision B, without a preservation argument or a renewed inspection. The escape clause is not decoration -- RENEWED INSPECTION DISCHARGES IT, and reading the final text once IS an adjudication. No impossibility is claimed here: an earlier draft said such a sweep can never close, and that was refuted, because renewed reading is the only mechanism that actually works. ",

    "RUNG: this form carries NONE. It is the sub-case the amended ceiling above excludes -- the subject is a written surface, so no input can be constructed to carry its extent, and the claim and the range remain two objects. ",

    "SPECIMEN ONE, three reviews that ranged over less than the row they reviewed: 5120939460, 5121228544 and 5121282475, none of which reached `test.claim.phantom_marker_type_argument_identity_witness` -- the file the row under repair CITES -- where two corrected-away formulations stood verbatim. The enumeration found them; no reviewer did. ",

    "SPECIMEN TWO, and it is what fixes the UNIT of repair: a repair landed at the QUOTED text, left the FRAMING sentence directly above it standing, and left a dependent two paragraphs BELOW it standing too -- one that never quoted the premise it rested on (`a trigger whose owner has ceased to exist is retired by nothing at all`). That dependent contained none of the repair's search terms precisely because it RESTED on the premise rather than quoting it. ",

    "So the unit of repair is the ENTAILMENT NEIGHBOURHOOD of the premise -- framing above, dependents below, sibling surfaces -- and it is BIDIRECTIONAL. A phrase-keyed sweep is keyed on quotation, and entailment does not quote. ",

    "REFUSED TRIGGER, recorded WITH its reason so it is not re-proposed: `enroll the sweep in CI`. Mechanisation moves the INVOCATION, not the SUBJECT -- the same incomplete phrase search would execute reliably over the same incomplete subject, so the trigger would fire while the capability stayed dead, which is exactly the DESIGN section 4b(3) grain mismatch between a loss sentence and its trigger. Rung 2 needs an adequate subject definition, a valid checking relation AND a consumer; automation supplies only the third. ",

    "THE NEIGHBOUR CHECKED AND EXCLUDED, using that row's own bounding text: selection_view_read_as_population is a set produced by a MEASUREMENT threshold and read as the population. Here nothing is measured and nothing is filtered -- the range was simply never as wide as the sentence beside it, which is this row's invariant, so the form is filed here and not minted. ",

    "The corroborating receipt from the row's own repair day: a phrase-keyed sweep certified that repair clean and missed four survivors, because the live one read `WHAT ACTUALLY HOLDS THIS CLASS AT 2` and matched none of the guessed patterns. The form applies to writing the form.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
